ame>YAMAMOTO VINITA CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO YASUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO VINITA CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, YASUJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO YASUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, YASUJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A high-efficiency thawing device for thawing a considerably thick, frozen object quickly and uniformly. High-frequency electric power from a high-frequency generator circuits (52, 62, 72) is supplied to pairs of electrodes (55a and 55b, 65a and 65b, 75a and 75b) through impedance-matching circuits (53, 63, 73) including transformers (54, 64, 74) so as to thaw a frozen object (F) placed between the electrodes by dielectric heating.  The impedance-matching circuits (53, 63, 73) comprise capacitance parts (C) and inductance parts (L), and the inductance parts (L) have conductors of graduated length, i.e., they are longer than those located in the upstream direction of the conveyer.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif de décongélation haute fréquence hautement efficace qui sert à décongeler un objet congelé d'une épaisseur considérable rapidement et de manière uniforme. Plusieurs paires d'électrodes (55a et 55b, 65a et 65b, 75a et 75b) sont alimentées en énergie électrique haute fréquence provenant de circuits générateurs de haute fréquence (52, 62, 72) à travers des circuits d'adaptation d'impédance (53, 63, 73) comprenant des transformateurs (54, 64, 74) de manière à décongeler par effet de chauffage du diélectrique un objet congelé (F) placé entre les électrodes. Les circuits d'adaptation d'impédance (53, 63, 73) comprennent des parties de capacitance (C) et d'inductance (L), ces dernières possédant des conducteurs à longueurs graduées qui sont plus longs que ceux placés en amont du convoyeur.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>